WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:07.935
Dick and Mr. Hobbs had written to Cedric about their ideas to help him.

2
00:00:07.936 --> 00:00:15.693
After that, they didn't know what else to do. But they had plenty to discuss.

3
00:00:15.694 --> 00:00:21.996
Every day the New York newspapers ran fresh stories about Cedric and the new Lord Fauntleroy.

4
00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:26.523
Every night Mr. Hobbs read the latest stories aloud to Dick.

5
00:00:26.524 --> 00:00:31.664
"It seems like this Earl of Dorincourt is an important guy," Dick said.

6
00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:36.847
"He's got tons of money, and his castle sounds like a grand place.

7
00:00:36.848 --> 00:00:41.278
Imagine our Cedric living in a fancy, old castle!"

8
00:00:41.279 --> 00:00:45.172
"Unfortunately, he may not be living there much longer."

9
00:00:45.173 --> 00:00:48.492
Mr. Hobbs put down the newspaper.

10
00:00:48.493 --> 00:00:55.743
"He's such a good kid. What's happened to him is a real shame."

11
00:00:55.744 --> 00:01:00.123
The next morning Dick was shining the boots of a regular customer.

12
00:01:00.124 --> 00:01:04.728
Mr. Bennington was a young man, just starting out as a lawyer.

13
00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:08.315
He always enjoyed talking to Dick.

14
00:01:08.316 --> 00:01:13.427
That day Mr. Bennington was reading a newspaper while Dick worked.

15
00:01:13.428 --> 00:01:15.958
"Have you heard about this earl in England?

16
00:01:15.959 --> 00:01:21.959
Turns out there are two kids, both claiming to be his heir. The Earl of Dorincourt—"

17
00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.856
"What?" Dick looked up from the man's boots in surprise.

18
00:01:26.857 --> 00:01:30.883
Mr. Bennington turned the paper so Dick could see a photo.

19
00:01:30.884 --> 00:01:35.759
"This is the new Lord Fauntleroy's mother. She's a handsome woman."

20
00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:42.420
Mr. Bennington noticed Dick's expression. "What's the matter with you?"

21
00:01:42.421 --> 00:01:46.520
Dick was staring wide-eyed and open-mouthed.

22
00:01:46.521 --> 00:01:50.837
He pointed to the woman, who had thick, dark hair.

23
00:01:50.838 --> 00:01:54.108
"I know her!" Dick said.

24
00:01:54.109 --> 00:02:00.111
"Sure you do." Mr. Bennington laughed.

25
00:02:00.112 --> 00:02:07.839
"And I'm best friends with the queen!" He shrugged as Dick continued to stare.

26
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.154
"I'm finished with the paper if you want it."

27
00:02:10.155 --> 00:02:15.836
"I do want it!" Dick hurriedly put away his cloths and polishes.

28
00:02:15.837 --> 00:02:18.832
"And I'm closing down the stand for the day!"

29
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:23.168
Mr. Bennington counted out the coins for his shoeshine.

30
00:02:23.169 --> 00:02:28.532
"I have no idea what's bothering you, but it sounds serious."

31
00:02:28.533 --> 00:02:34.499
A few minutes later, Dick was racing through the streets toward Mr. Hobbs' store.

32
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.897
Dick was so out of breath that he could hardly speak.

33
00:02:37.898 --> 00:02:45.701
"Look . . . at . . . this . . ." He handed the newspaper to Mr. Hobbs.

34
00:02:45.702 --> 00:02:50.500
"What am I looking at?" Mr. Hobbs put down his broom.

35
00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:53.741
"The woman in this picture!" Dick shouted.

36
00:02:53.742 --> 00:02:58.893
"She's no lord's wife! That's Minna—my brother's wife!

37
00:02:58.894 --> 00:03:02.630
I'd know her anywhere, and so would Ben."

38
00:03:02.631 --> 00:03:07.612
Mr. Hobbs dropped into his chair and studied the newspaper.

39
00:03:07.613 --> 00:03:14.081
"I was right! Those aristocrats have cheated Cedric out of his title!"

40
00:03:14.082 --> 00:03:21.014
"No, Minna is the one who's cheated Cedric." Dick stamped his foot in anger.

41
00:03:21.015 --> 00:03:25.453
"As soon as I saw her picture, I remembered another story we'd read.

42
00:03:25.454 --> 00:03:30.595
It mentioned that the new Lord Fauntleroy has a scar on his chin."

43
00:03:30.596 --> 00:03:37.043
"Just like your nephew!" Mr. Hobbs was now as angry as Dick.

44
00:03:37.044 --> 00:03:42.201
"That's right! Tom got that scar when Minna threw the plate.

45
00:03:42.202 --> 00:03:46.529
He's no more Lord Fauntleroy than I am," Dick said.

46
00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.575
"We have to do something right now!"

47
00:03:49.576 --> 00:03:56.508
Mr. Hobbs sank into his chair, overwhelmed by the problem, but Dick was full of energy.

48
00:03:56.509 --> 00:04:01.413
"Hand me some scissors, so I can cut out this picture," Dick said.

49
00:04:01.414 --> 00:04:04.885
"I'm going to send it to Ben."

50
00:04:04.886 --> 00:04:09.009
"I'll write to Cedric—and the earl."

51
00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:13.769
They were in the midst of their letters when Dick had another idea.

52
00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:19.311
"That guy who gave me the newspaper is a lawyer. Maybe he can help us."

53
00:04:19.312 --> 00:04:23.715
Mr. Hobbs was immediately impressed by Dick's suggestion.

54
00:04:23.716 --> 00:04:29.677
"You're absolutely right. This situation calls for a lawyer."

55
00:04:29.678 --> 00:04:35.379
Mr. Bennington was surprised when Dick and Mr. Hobbs arrived at his office.

56
00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:41.094
"You've already shined my boots once today," Mr. Bennington said with a smile.

57
00:04:41.095 --> 00:04:43.977
"Are you looking for more customers?"

58
00:04:43.978 --> 00:04:47.917
"This is my friend Mr. Hobbs, and we need your help," Dick said.

59
00:04:47.918 --> 00:04:50.721
"It's about that newspaper story."

60
00:04:50.722 --> 00:04:55.376
He quickly described how Cedric had become Lord Fauntleroy.

61
00:04:55.377 --> 00:05:01.109
Mr. Bennington took notes as Dick talked about Minna and her son, Tom.

62
00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:07.373
"I've read about this woman before. Parts of her story don't make sense."

63
00:05:07.374 --> 00:05:10.987
Mr. Bennington tapped his pen on his desk.

64
00:05:10.988 --> 00:05:13.624
"There's no harm in investigating this.

65
00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:18.123
I'm not busy right now, and the publicity may give my career a boost."

66
00:05:18.124 --> 00:05:26.102
"I don't care what you charge," Mr. Hobbs said. "Send me the bill, and I'll gladly pay it."

67
00:05:26.103 --> 00:05:31.928
"My first task is to write to Dick's brother, Ben, and to the earl's lawyer."

68
00:05:31.929 --> 00:05:35.950
Mr. Bennington pulled out some paper.

69
00:05:35.951 --> 00:05:41.089
When the two friends left Mr. Bennington's office, they were full of hope.

70
00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:48.007
At midnight Dick and Mr. Hobbs were still talking in the grocery store.

71
00:05:48.008 --> 00:05:53.570
One of Mr. Bennington's letters was on a train speeding westward.

72
00:05:53.571 --> 00:05:59.604
The other was on a ship sailing eastward for England.

